    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "value": {
        "level": "1",
        "content": "Operating Earnings Yield"
      },
      "id": "2fabd9cb-e07a-44f8-9827-a2c73ecaf0ba"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"8i6gi\"><b>Hypothesis</b></p><p data-block-key=\"t0p46\">If the operating income of a company is currently higher than its past 1 year history, buy the company’s stock and vice-versa.</p><p data-block-key=\"3q032\"></p><p data-block-key=\"tw4vi\"><b>Implementation</b></p><p data-block-key=\"u0gl1\">Using ts_rank to identify current performance of the company compared to its own history, using the fundamental data field &quot;operating_income&quot;.</p><p data-block-key=\"gik4s\"></p><p data-block-key=\"o4qvs\"><b>Hints to Implement</b></p><p data-block-key=\"3nwh7\">Rather than comparing the value directly, can calculating a ratio that includes stock market moves, improve the signal?</p>",
      "id": "16c67205-f1a8-4d14-8128-69c67c8d7b88"
    },
    {
      "type": "SIMULATION_EXAMPLE",
      "value": {
        "settings": {
          "instrumentType": "EQUITY",
          "region": "USA",
          "universe": "TOP3000",
          "delay": 1,
          "decay": 0,
          "neutralization": "SUBINDUSTRY",
          "truncation": 0.08,
          "pasteurization": "ON",
          "unitHandling": "VERIFY",
          "nanHandling": "OFF",
          "language": "FASTEXPR",
          "maxTrade": "OFF"
        },
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "regular": "ts_rank(operating_income,252)"
      },
      "id": "c8147118-4226-4621-a768-3d523b8287db"
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "value": {
        "level": "1",
        "content": "Appreciation of liabilities"
      },
      "id": "937878a5-f302-43a4-8cbc-b7ad1c6dbd20"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"tzore\"><b>Hypothesis</b></p><p data-block-key=\"8ichr\">An increase in the fair value of liabilities could indicate a higher cost than expected. This may deteriorate the company&#x27;s financial health, potentially leading to lower profitability or financial distress.</p><p data-block-key=\"mogf1\"></p><p data-block-key=\"s507y\"><b>Implementation</b></p><p data-block-key=\"j7vg5\">Go short when there is an increase in the fair value of liabilities within a year and long when the opposite occurs using fundamental data.</p><p data-block-key=\"ja86o\"></p><p data-block-key=\"3op6p\"><b>Hints to Implement</b></p><p data-block-key=\"bgorq\">Could observing the increase over a shorter period improve accuracy?</p>",
      "id": "b9d5d4c7-8238-44dc-a32d-942191624b48"
    },
    {
      "type": "SIMULATION_EXAMPLE",
      "value": {
        "settings": {
          "instrumentType": "EQUITY",
          "region": "USA",
          "universe": "TOP3000",
          "delay": 1,
          "decay": 0,
          "neutralization": "SUBINDUSTRY",
          "truncation": 0.08,
          "pasteurization": "ON",
          "unitHandling": "VERIFY",
          "nanHandling": "OFF",
          "language": "FASTEXPR",
          "maxTrade": "OFF"
        },
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "regular": "-ts_rank(fn_liab_fair_val_l1_a,252)"
      },
      "id": "fa0865b4-3080-466a-b77d-25b90713df0b"
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "value": {
        "level": "1",
        "content": "Power of leverage"
      },
      "id": "c4c57a62-fa49-4c75-bff0-87222f4bb794"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"b8bh0\"><b>Hypothesis</b></p><p data-block-key=\"d80u0\">Companies with high liability-to-asset ratios – excluding those with poor financial health or weak cashflows – often leverage debt as a strategic tool to pursue aggressive growth initiatives. By effectively utilizing financial leverage, these firms are more likely to deliver outsized returns, as they reinvest borrowed capital into high-potential opportunities.</p><p data-block-key=\"0pyq7\"><br/><b>Implementation</b></p><p data-block-key=\"dgssr\">Use the ‘liabilities’ and ‘assets’ to design the ratio.</p><p data-block-key=\"b2e2i\"><br/><b>Hint to improve the Alpha</b></p><p data-block-key=\"ewzeh\">This ratio can vary significantly across industries. Would it be worth considering alternative neutralization settings?</p>",
      "id": "fe2b8127-17e6-4b86-bce6-185c95d6c1ef"
    },
    {
      "type": "SIMULATION_EXAMPLE",
      "value": {
        "settings": {
          "instrumentType": "EQUITY",
          "region": "USA",
          "universe": "TOP3000",
          "delay": 1,
          "decay": 0,
          "neutralization": "MARKET",
          "truncation": 0.01,
          "pasteurization": "ON",
          "unitHandling": "VERIFY",
          "nanHandling": "OFF",
          "language": "FASTEXPR",
          "maxTrade": "OFF"
        },
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "regular": "liabilities/assets"
      },
      "id": "bb4244b9-bdd2-40ef-bb86-284acf6cc8e1"
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "value": {
        "level": "1",
        "content": "Earnings Yield Momentum"
      },
      "id": "40ff6f66-263e-4d6c-9b32-7ce0867f7d5d"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"iikpi\"><b>Hypothesis</b></p><p data-block-key=\"unrc2\">Stocks whose earnings yield has been high more often over the last quarter, relative to their own history, may be undervalued thus we should long them</p><p data-block-key=\"jbfyj\"><br/><b>Implementation</b></p><p data-block-key=\"su9c2\">Use EPS-to-price ratio as earnings yield proxy, compare over its own past, and compare it within its industry.</p><p data-block-key=\"wwemx\"><br/><b>Hint to improve the Alpha</b></p><p data-block-key=\"akmnq\">Use NAN HANDLING to preprocess data and boost the performance</p>",
      "id": "d7cc0195-d7cd-4ab2-99ba-2594d226db2a"
    },
    {
      "type": "SIMULATION_EXAMPLE",
      "value": {
        "settings": {
          "instrumentType": "EQUITY",
          "region": "USA",
          "universe": "TOP3000",
          "delay": 1,
          "decay": 0,
          "neutralization": "INDUSTRY",
          "truncation": 0.08,
          "pasteurization": "ON",
          "unitHandling": "VERIFY",
          "nanHandling": "OFF",
          "language": "FASTEXPR",
          "maxTrade": "OFF"
        },
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "regular": "group_rank(ts_rank(est_eps/close, 60),industry)"
      },
      "id": "18891d47-fa6c-4955-8f13-29cfc2157965"
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "value": {
        "level": "1",
        "content": "Short-Term Sentiment Volume Stability"
      },
      "id": "7ce17b0d-2b62-4e3f-bacb-9ea79d2c98b3"
    },
    {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "value": "<p data-block-key=\"jtwx4\"><b>Hypothesis</b></p><p data-block-key=\"v07rr\">A high 10-day standard deviation of sentiment volume for a stock means that investor attention is unstable, with frequent spikes and drops in how much the stock is discussed. This unstable attention is often driven by short-lived news or hype and may lead to noisy, unsustainable price moves, causing the stock to underperform afterward.</p><p data-block-key=\"fvxdr\"><br/><b>Implementation</b></p><p data-block-key=\"uyt0u\">Take the 10-day rolling standard deviation of relative sentiment volume scl12_buzz and negate it.</p><p data-block-key=\"5hfou\"><br/><b>Hint to improve the Alpha</b></p><p data-block-key=\"czzjw\">Would observing stability over a shorter horizon be more effective for more liquid stocks?</p>",
      "id": "a76bd579-7818-46cb-a2ec-771c3359a80a"
    },
    {
      "type": "SIMULATION_EXAMPLE",
      "value": {
        "settings": {
          "instrumentType": "EQUITY",
          "region": "USA",
          "universe": "TOP3000",
          "delay": 1,
          "decay": 0,
          "neutralization": "INDUSTRY",
          "truncation": 0.08,
          "pasteurization": "ON",
          "unitHandling": "VERIFY",
          "nanHandling": "OFF",
          "language": "FASTEXPR",
          "maxTrade": "OFF"
        },
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "regular": "-ts_std_dev(scl12_buzz, 10)"
      },
      "id": "3363dc2a-24f3-4500-a963-faf021ed23fc"
    }
